  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A parallel plate capacitor is made up of stair like structure with a plate area A of each stair and that is connected with a wire of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>, as shown in the figure. The capacitance of the arrangement is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0071_f2eda99e6fb4.png\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 208px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "23",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0071_6c369f647f1d.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 128px;\" /></p><p>Here the system can be considered as three capacitors in parallel.</p><p>So, net capacitance is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>23</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}